WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
Hi

2
00:00:01.748 --> 00:00:02.823
Oh my goodness.

3
00:00:02.823 --> 00:00:04.410
I have never seen another person

4
00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:06.133
hold my book until this moment,

5
00:00:06.133 --> 00:00:08.150
until I was like oh my God

6
00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:09.180
the first time I'm seeing someone

7
00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:11.810
hold my book it's Drew Barrymore.

8
00:00:11.810 --> 00:00:13.136
Oh my gosh I'm not kidding.

9
00:00:13.136 --> 00:00:16.270
When we first started the show and I wanted to

10
00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:18.927
describe the conversations that I wanted to have.

11
00:00:18.927 --> 00:00:20.830
I kept talking about you.

12
00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:23.060
I'm such a longtime fan,

13
00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:27.420
and your poetry is so important and meaningful,

14
00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:32.230
and you have hooked so many people with it with poetry.

15
00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:34.146
And I just think that it's so extraordinary.

16
00:00:34.146 --> 00:00:37.210
Do you have any objectivity on why

17
00:00:37.210 --> 00:00:39.892
what you put out there resonates so much with people?

18
00:00:39.892 --> 00:00:44.892
You know, I think that poetry in general is the easiest

19
00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:48.970
and can at times maybe be the freest form of therapy

20
00:00:48.970 --> 00:00:50.520
a person can get that day

21
00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:52.250
because for the most part

22
00:00:52.250 --> 00:00:55.590
it's a really emotion focused way of communicating.

23
00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:58.300
And there's so many spaces where they tell us

24
00:00:58.300 --> 00:00:59.570
don't bring your emotions.

25
00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:00.680
You know, don't be emotional.

26
00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:02.170
I think especially as women we've cut

27
00:01:02.170 --> 00:01:05.440
off so much of ourselves in order to try to progress

28
00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:06.579
into certain spaces

29
00:01:06.579 --> 00:01:08.650
and that's changing a lot now.

30
00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:11.420
But I think that poetry as always saying like,

31
00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:13.190
your heart belongs in this room,

32
00:01:13.190 --> 00:01:14.940
your heart belongs in this conversation.

33
00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:17.480
Your heart belongs in this communication.

34
00:01:17.480 --> 00:01:20.110
And so, you know I just feel so grateful

35
00:01:20.110 --> 00:01:21.320
that people have allowed

36
00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:24.600
for my poetry to maybe be an entry point

37
00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:27.780
into going into the genre at all.

38
00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:29.110
I have so many people who are like,

39
00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:31.620
I hated poetry but I loved Heart Talk,

40
00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:34.420
or you know I never thought I'd like it or get into it.

41
00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:36.540
And I think that for me you know,

42
00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:38.760
whether it's through my writing for poetry

43
00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:40.617
or activism in any form.

44
00:01:40.617 --> 00:01:44.143
I'm always just looking for the easiest on-ramp,

45
00:01:44.143 --> 00:01:47.100
or entry point to get people involved

46
00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:49.260
and in touch with themselves.

47
00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:53.090
Well you have a beautiful new daughter, Memphis.

48
00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:53.923
Yes.

49
00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:58.670
And you dedicated this book to her?

50
00:01:58.670 --> 00:02:00.791
And by the way I love your man, Simon.

51
00:02:00.791 --> 00:02:02.640
I was lucky enough to work

52
00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:04.423
with him on Charlie's angels,

53
00:02:05.270 --> 00:02:06.390
back in the day.

54
00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:09.720
And now you have this beautiful new daughter together.

55
00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:11.840
Memphis who's just turned a year.

56
00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:13.180
Is that correct?

57
00:02:13.180 --> 00:02:16.343
Yeah she's about a year and two months so.

58
00:02:18.295 --> 00:02:21.760
And now you wrote this beautiful new children's book.

59
00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:23.540
I can't think of a better pairing

60
00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:25.810
than Cleo Wade and a children's book.

61
00:02:25.810 --> 00:02:27.623
It's called What The Road Said.

62
00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:31.937
May I ask again what your light bulb moment was

63
00:02:31.937 --> 00:02:34.685
for creating this book?

64
00:02:34.685 --> 00:02:38.500
You know when I first started the journey of this book

65
00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:42.070
it's so interesting because I really started writing it,

66
00:02:42.070 --> 00:02:43.410
I think for my childhood self.

67
00:02:43.410 --> 00:02:47.130
I wasn't pregnant when I started this book.

68
00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:48.590
And I really you know,

69
00:02:48.590 --> 00:02:51.140
I just remember in my own childhood just feeling

70
00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:54.280
like there was so many times where I felt so alone,

71
00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:56.660
or there were these really big questions I had

72
00:02:56.660 --> 00:02:58.330
and no one really had the answers

73
00:02:58.330 --> 00:03:00.010
to them or was even afraid to voice them.

74
00:03:00.010 --> 00:03:02.150
And I wondered if there was more out there.

75
00:03:02.150 --> 00:03:03.830
I wondered how to use my voice.

76
00:03:03.830 --> 00:03:06.550
I wondered how to find or understand bravery

77
00:03:06.550 --> 00:03:09.130
or vulnerability or all these things that we still

78
00:03:09.130 --> 00:03:10.320
even struggle with as adults.

79
00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:12.499
And so I wanted to write something that was

80
00:03:12.499 --> 00:03:16.620
like a healing balm to my childhood self.

81
00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:21.620
And then halfway through the process I got pregnant,

82
00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:25.780
and it was so crazy because this journey that started

83
00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:29.208
for my own childhood healing ended up

84
00:03:29.208 --> 00:03:32.220
becoming a book for my daughter.

85
00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:34.150
And so the this book is so personal

86
00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:36.630
and so emotional for me.

87
00:03:36.630 --> 00:03:39.140
I seriously I still I've been started doing interviews

88
00:03:39.140 --> 00:03:40.210
about it like two weeks ago.

89
00:03:40.210 --> 00:03:44.810
And I almost cry every time because you know it really is.

90
00:03:44.810 --> 00:03:48.142
It's everything you know it's every

91
00:03:48.142 --> 00:03:51.654
thing I hope my daughter can know in her life.

92
00:03:51.654 --> 00:03:54.890
And it's everything I hope that every young girl

93
00:03:54.890 --> 00:03:56.870
or young person you know,

94
00:03:56.870 --> 00:04:00.460
it's something I wish they could all have truly.

95
00:04:00.460 --> 00:04:01.650
I'm so proud of this.

96
00:04:01.650 --> 00:04:04.383
And so it's a really emotional book for me,

97
00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:08.230
but I'm so excited to put it put it out.

98
00:04:08.230 --> 00:04:11.690
Well, I'm sure your daughter will marvel

99
00:04:11.690 --> 00:04:14.640
with parents like you and Simon.

100
00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:17.130
And I think that we're all looking

101
00:04:17.130 --> 00:04:18.590
for the takeaways in life.

102
00:04:18.590 --> 00:04:20.050
It's so important.

103
00:04:20.050 --> 00:04:22.313
And your work is so full of them.

104
00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:24.703
Thank you so much.

105
00:04:26.768 --> 00:04:29.570
Um I just can't even believe you just said that to me.

106
00:04:29.570 --> 00:04:31.220
So thank you so much.

107
00:04:31.220 --> 00:04:34.130
Thank you so much Cleo Wade for coming here to talk

108
00:04:34.130 --> 00:04:35.530
about your children's book,

109
00:04:35.530 --> 00:04:37.120
which I again was like,

110
00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:39.326
oh that's the most potent combination.

111
00:04:39.326 --> 00:04:42.310
What The Road Said is available now

112
00:04:42.310 --> 00:04:45.400
in stores and online wherever books are sold.

113
00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:46.770
Thank you so much.

114
00:04:46.770 --> 00:04:48.510
Say hi to Simon and,

115
00:04:48.510 --> 00:04:49.460
I will!

116
00:04:49.460 --> 00:04:51.939
And hello to beautiful Memphis.

117
00:04:51.939 --> 00:04:55.022
(upbeat outro music)

